  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nAbove Normal Temps and Dry Conditions: The upper low out west\nwill begin to shift northeast into the northern plains as\nanother low moves into the northwest US on Monday and Tuesday.\nThis low then moves into the northern plains mid week, placing \nour area in more of a southwest flow. The lack of moisture and \nlift should keep the persistence forecast going for much of next\nweek with highs in the 70s and lows in the 50s. The warmest \ndays of the week (higher chances of at least reaching 80) appear\nto be around Thursday as even warm air aloft moves in ahead of\nthe next system. Precipitation chances remain less than 10 \npercent through Friday.\n\nRain Chances Next Weekend: While significant ensemble variance\nremains, the southwest flow pattern aloft looks to allow for at\nleast some rain chances for next weekend. The main questions\ncenter around the upper low out west and its path and timing.\nEnsemble cluster analysis does suggest the rain potential \nincreasing and rain chances are now in the 30-50% range for next\nweekend.",
